title: Codex frontend hook self-registers a second alias alongside the managed launcher alias (dual-identity)
updated_at: "2026-07-11T16:22:49Z"
---
A managed 'c2c new/start codex' session registers a launcher alias, but the stock codex frontend's own 'c2c hook codex' (SessionStart) ALSO auto-registers a separate alias for the same session -> two identities per session. Pre-existing frontend-env gap surfaced during B131 live E2E; disclosed as a caveat in docs/client-delivery.md. Fix direction: have the frontend hook detect it is inside a managed app-server session (same signals B136 added in codex_session_is_managed: C2C_MCP_SESSION_ID / thread->instance mapping / codex-app-server registration) and adopt the launcher alias instead of self-registering a new one. Add an E2E asserting exactly one alias per managed session.